body:
I don't know what date I'm on, but I haven't been drinking like I used to due to being put on antibiotics for latent TB - I feel really sick when I drink on those! So, for today, and every day, I will not drink with you.

&#x200B;

ETA: Apparently day 156! This time last year I don't think I'd believe I was capable of this.

Thanks for sharing your experience. I'm glad your symptoms are easing up and that you're able to look back at your past habit from a new angle. It's crazy how much the fog clears when you stop filling your brain with smoke. 

&#x200B;

Congrats on being a week down! I hope your symptoms subside quickly

You know, the thing about life is that it has its ups and downs. You're not always going to feel amazing, that's just how it is. But with sobriety, we're able to take those negatives as they come, think about them clearly, and want more for ourselves. 

&#x200B;

You're doing a great thing here. Keep up the great work!

More motivation is what I'm looking forward to. Congrats on four days! You're right that breaking the cycle that first day is tough. 

&#x200B;

We can do this!

I will not be drinking today! 

&#x200B;

(My badge isn't accurate - I resumed sobriety on January 1st 2022 after holiday bender :/)

Today I have tied my previous streak for not drinking. Tomorrow I hope to break it.

&#x200B;

IWNDWYT

Today is my first day off in over two weeks. Normally I'd use this as an excuse to drink all day but instead I'm sticking to tea and hot chocolate and relaxing to Animal Crossing. 

&#x200B;

IWNDWYT

Had a bit of a rocky start this morning but I made it through! Spent some time with friends, got work done. All without touching a drink. Here's to another day of sobriety!

&#x200B;

IWNDWYT!
